{"title":"Career Roadmap · Resident Doctor","role":"Resident Doctor","summary":"A Resident Doctor is a qualified medical graduate undergoing structured postgraduate clinical training or working in a hospital-based residency role under the supervision and responsibility framework applicable to the institution and current medical regulations.","facts":{"Current degree":"MBBS (Bachelor of Medicine & Bachelor of Surgery)","Course":"MBBS"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Resident Doctor is a qualified medical graduate undergoing structured postgraduate clinical training or working in a hospital-based residency role under the supervision and responsibility framework applicable to the institution and current medical regulations."},{"type":"p","text":"Resident doctors are central to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient assessment"},{"text":"Clinical history and examination"},{"text":"Diagnosis and differential diagnosis"},{"text":"Investigations"},{"text":"Treatment planning"},{"text":"Emergency care"},{"text":"Ward management"},{"text":"Outpatient care"},{"text":"Procedures"},{"text":"Surgical assistance where applicable"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Interdisciplinary coordination"},{"text":"Follow-up care"},{"text":"Clinical research and academic activities"},{"text":"The career is highly patient-facing, evidence-based and responsibility-intensive."}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"In India, MBBS provides the foundation for medical practice subject to current registration/licensing requirements. “Resident Doctor” can refer to different institutional roles, including junior residency after MBBS and postgraduate residency during MD/MS or equivalent training. Exact eligibility, registration and appointment requirements vary by institution and current regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class